# Baseline artefacts are compared byte-for-byte, so git must not touch them.
#
# core.autocrlf is on, which means a fresh clone would rewrite every LF in these
# files to CRLF and change every sha256 — including the ones the checker's
# reproduction step diffs against. Generation is not reproducible run to run, so
# a rewritten artefact cannot be regenerated back to its verified bytes.
#
# -text disables all end-of-line conversion for these paths in both directions.
archive/** -text
out/**     -text

# Everything else normalises as usual: LF in the repository, native on checkout.
